2h35m 2026-08-01-Sat-W30
  [^] 05:15 2h35m <env> FIND: WTF why my wifi is only 24MiB/s ⌇⡪⡮⣌⠇
    INFO: Intel AX201 is a 2x2 (2-stream) WiFi 6 adapter — max theoretical 5GHz
    link rate ~1200 Mbps (MCS11, 2SS, 80MHz, 1024-QAM), but that's negotiated
    with a WiFi 6 AP. Against your RT-AC68U (WiFi 5/AC only, no 802.11ax),
    it'll connect at up to 866 Mbps PHY rate (AC, 2SS, 80MHz).
    :Practical throughput: expect roughly 400-550 Mbps real-world on a good link.
      $ lspci -k | grep -A3 -i network
      $ sudo lspci -vvv -s 0000:00:14.3
      $ iw phy
      $ iw dev wlan0 link
      $ ethtool enp67s0
    PERF
      #fra $ iperf3 -s
      #hpx $ iperf3 -c 192.168.1.4 -t 30 -i 5 --bidir
    INFO: Connected to 10:c3:7b:55:63:94 (on wlan0)
      SSID: home5
      freq: 5500.0
      RX: 7396145 bytes (14503 packets)
      TX: 1500859 bytes (12520 packets)
      signal: -47 dBm
      rx bitrate: 433.3 MBit/s VHT-MCS 9 80MHz short GI VHT-NSS 1
      tx bitrate: 234.0 MBit/s VHT-MCS 3 80MHz VHT-NSS 2
      bss flags: short-slot-time
      dtim period: 3
      beacon int: 100
      ---
        Now you're on 5GHz, and this is informative: RX is NSS 1 (single
        stream, 433.3 Mbit/s) but TX is NSS 2 (dual stream, but only MCS3 = 234
        Mbit/s). That asymmetry means the link isn't running at full 2x2
        quality in both directions — likely a weaker path or interference on
        the router's RX side, despite your strong -47 dBm signal.
         Max you should be seeing with a clean 2x2 link at 80MHz/short-GI is
         866.7 Mbit/s (VHT-MCS9, NSS2) — you're getting roughly half that on RX,
         and TX is stuck at a low MCS despite using both streams.
        Worth checking: watch -n1 'iw dev wlan0 link' to see if rates fluctuate —
        could indicate intermittent interference (2.4GHz/microwave/neighbors)
        rather than a hard ceiling.
         Related if relevant: forcing/checking 80MHz channel isn't overlapping
         with neighbors (iw dev wlan0 scan for co-channel APs), driver
         power-save (iw dev wlan0 get power_save) throttling iwlwifi, physical
         obstruction/angle to router antennas.
    [✓] TODO: plug pc into LAN
      [✗] INFO: (b) Transfer through both simultaneously (link aggregation/bonding) —
        not possible here. Bonding/LACP requires the switch/router to support 802.3ad on its ports;
        the RT-AC68U's switch doesn't support LACP. Without router-side support,
        you can't combine WiFi + Ethernet bandwidth for a single transfer to one peer.
      $ sudo ethtool enp67s0 | grep -iE "speed|duplex"
        Speed: 1000Mb/s
        Duplex: Full
      $ ip -s link show enp67s0
      $ ethtool -S enp67s0 | grep -iE "error|crc|drop|discard|fifo|frame" Gv '0$'
       rx_crc_errors: 2431
       rx_errors: 2885
